note Nominal seal: the operand calls run in source order before the holds check, and a failing check
note traps 10 (exit 110) after both calls ran. The first constructor call passes (trace 21: hi32 then
note lo32); the boundary values 0 and 0xffffffff pass; one byte is written to stdout (so a check that fires
note early is visible); the second call breaks the invariant and traps.
om2
abstract dup32 ulong ops xor
holds dup32 dup32
global tr ulong 1
global bump ulong 1
fn hi32 x uint to ulong
put tr 0 add mul get tr 0 10 2
ret ulong x
end
fn lo32 x uint to ulong
put tr 0 add mul get tr 0 10 1
ret add ulong x get bump 0
end
fn dup32mk x uint to dup32
ret seal dup32 or shl hi32 x 32 lo32 x
end
fn main to int
a = dup32mk 7
if ne get tr 0 21
ret 1
end
if ne open a 0x0000000700000007
ret 2
end
z = dup32mk 0
m = dup32mk 0xffffffff
if ne open xor z m 0xffffffffffffffff
ret 3
end
if ne open xor m m 0
ret 4
end
buf = new uchar 1 79
w = write 1 buf 0 1
put bump 0 1
b = dup32mk 5
ret 5
end
